  "body": "## What changed\n- `AGENTS.md`, release cut: new **step 5, \"Check the documentation site\"**. The tag run's `site` and `pages` jobs in `release.yml` regenerate and deploy the Zola site from the tagged tree (`pages` waits for `publish`), with the browser build under `/app/` (#1103). The cut is done once `pages` is green and the live site shows \"CamCraft X.Y.Z\"; a red `pages` job is re-run, never fixed by moving the tag. Nothing is committed for the site and no trigger is added.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 53 -> 54 (process file changed).\n- `docs/decisions/688-release-site-step.md`: the decision.\n\nThis is the last open \"Done means\" item of #688. The rest already shipped: the Zola site in `site/` builds locally (`zola build`, PR #777), the release tag regenerates and publishes it to Pages (maintainer comment, 2026-11-12), it shows the version and links to the release downloads (`site/templates/index.html`, `base.html`), and the browser build is served under `/app/` (#1103, closed).\n\n## How tested\nDocs/process only. `cargo xtask gate quick` plan: nothing in `crates/` changed, no tests to run. Read the new step against `release.yml` (jobs `site`, `wasm`, `pages`, `publish`) and `site/README.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo tag run; the step describes the existing workflow, it does not change it. The Actions minutes the site adds to a tag run (an open question on the issue) are not measured here.\n\n## Process change\n`PROCESS_VERSION 54`: AGENTS.md cut step 5 (site check). A fork needs nothing beyond the usual process-file sync; its own tag runs deploy to its own Pages URL.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #688\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
